##THREADS ACCOUNT SETUP 
Once you've selected your niche, the next step is to create a dedicated Threads account that represents your ebook business. Your profile acts as a landing page, so it should clearly communicate what you offer and encourage visitors to explore your products.



Create a Dedicated Account - 
Create a separate Instagram account for your ebook business rather than using your personal account.
Set up a Threads profile using that Instagram account.
Choose a username related to your niche.



Set Up Your Profile - 
Username: Choose a simple, memorable username related to your niche.
Display Name: Use your name or pen name along with your niche (e.g., Alex Rivera | Digital Marketing).
Profile Picture: Use a clear, professional headshot or a consistent brand identity.
Bio: Write a short bio that explains what you offer, who you help and what value people can expect.



Optimize Your Bio - 

Your bio should communicate three things:
Credibility: Establish why people should trust your content.
Value Proposition: Explain what problem you help your audience solve.
Call to Action (CTA): Encourage visitors to check out your ebook or product link.

Example:
Helping students build better careers. Practical guides for internships and skill development. Get the complete guide below ↓



Add Your Product Link - 
Once your ebook is ready and uploaded to Gumroad, copy its product link.
Open your Threads profile and select Edit Profile.
Add your Gumroad product link to the Links section.
Make sure the link works and directs visitors to the correct product page.



Things to Keep in Mind - 
Keep your username consistent across Instagram, Threads and Gumroad where possible.
Maintain a professional and recognizable profile.
Avoid complicated usernames and lengthy bios.
Make your bio audience-focused rather than simply describing yourself.
Don't make claims about experience or results that you cannot support.
Keep your profile link updated when launching new products.
